# Features the tests' workspace build turns on and a published build (scripts/oci_build.sh, one cargo run per
# image) does not, each read and found to change nothing the binary does: scripts/check_standalone_features.sh
# fails on any difference not listed here. One line each: the published build (its packages joined by "+", as
# the check prints them, or * for every build) and crate/feature. A feature a binary needs is not listed: it is
# declared in that crate's Cargo.toml. `scripts/check_standalone_features.sh --print` lists every difference.
#
# Read for 0.2.9 (Rust 1.98, Cargo.lock of 2026-11-03).

# Only API: trait impls (std::error::Error, Debug/Eq, io::Write, From), types and constructors no published
# binary calls; a binary that called one would not compile without the feature.
* aead/alloc
* aead/default
* aead/getrandom
* aead/rand_core
* aes-gcm/alloc
* aes-gcm/default
* aes-gcm/getrandom
* aes-gcm/rand_core
* arrayvec/std
* chacha20poly1305/default
* chacha20poly1305/getrandom
* chacha20poly1305/rand_core
* crypto-common/getrandom
* crypto-common/std
* derive_more/from_str
* derive_more/into_iterator
* derive_more-impl/from_str
* derive_more-impl/into_iterator
* digest/block-buffer
* digest/core-api
* digest/mac
* digest/oid
* digest/std
* digest/subtle
* displaydoc/default
* displaydoc/std
* ed25519/alloc
* ed25519/pem
* ed25519/pkcs8
* ed25519/std
* ed25519-dalek/alloc
* ed25519-dalek/pem
* ed25519-dalek/pkcs8
* ed25519-dalek/std
* getrandom/std
* getrandom/sys_rng
* hashbrown/default-hasher
* hashbrown/raw
* iroh-base/default
* libc/extra_traits
* rand_core/getrandom
* reqwest/json
* reqwest/stream
* ring/std
* serde_core/alloc
* serde_core/rc
* serde_core/result
* sha2/default
* sha2/std
* signature/alloc
* signature/std
* time/formatting
* time/macros
* time/parsing
* toml_datetime/serde
* zerocopy/simd

# The relay server and its metrics service (iroh-relay/server, iroh-metrics/service), which only the built-in
# Stream relay runs and xbt-stream-relay declares; the other builds use iroh-relay's client. tokio/signal comes
# with the server. noq's platform-verifier adds a verifier iroh uses only when asked (CaTlsConfig::system),
# which no crate here does: iroh keeps its embedded roots either way. HTTP/2 in hyper comes from igd-next (UPnP
# port mapping), which the relay's build does not use.
* iroh-relay/server
* iroh-metrics/service
* tokio/signal
* tokio/signal-hook-registry
* noq/platform-verifier
* noq-proto/platform-verifier
* hyper/http2
* hyper-util/http2

# Counters only: without them iroh's metrics are not counted (nothing here reads them, except the relay, which
# declares them).
* iroh-relay/metrics
* iroh-metrics/metrics

# Speed only, the same results: inlining (hashbrown), run-time CPU detection for SIMD (memchr, simdutf8).
* hashbrown/inline-more
* memchr/default
* simdutf8/default

# Logging only: tracing-core's std (per-thread dispatch; the binaries set one global subscriber or none),
# tracing's log bridge, noq-udp's log output.
* tracing-core/default
* tracing/log
* noq-udp/default
* noq-udp/tracing-log

# Wiping the stream cipher's state when it is dropped (chacha20, cipher). Hygiene, not function: a binary works
# the same without it. Kept as a difference for now; declare it on the crates that hold long-lived keys if wanted.
* chacha20/zeroize
* cipher/zeroize

# xbt402's HTTP client for the seller gateway: an API it does not call. The 0.2.7 gateway image, built without it,
# passed every gateway check of packaging/linux/test-linux.sh on the published images. (xbt-hashlink, which also
# lacked it, now declares it: see crates/xbt-hashlink/Cargo.toml.)
xbt-gateway xbt402/http-client
